---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy · My Family Allowance">
  <Fragment slot="nav">
    <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" href="/">Home</a>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: October 26, 2026</p>

    <p>
      My Family Allowance is a small family money tracker. This page explains what
      information the app stores and how it is used.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Parents sign in with an email and password, and kids use a username and password.
      We store salted one-way password hashes, not the original passwords.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the app, we also store the family data you enter: kids’ names,
      allowance amounts, balances, transaction memos, your family page URL slug,
      monthly spending amounts, usernames, and salted password hashes.
    </p>

    <p>We also store hashed client-address identifiers and short-window attempt counters to limit password guessing.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use this information only to run the service: keep you signed in, show
      your family’s balances, and credit monthly allowance on schedule. We do not
      sell personal data or use it for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and sessions</h2>
    <p>
      After sign-in, a secure session cookie remembers your parent or kid account
      for up to seven days. Changing a password or disabling kid sign-in invalidates
      that account’s existing sessions.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see family data</h2>
    <p>
      Only the initial parent and parents added by an existing parent can manage family data.
      Each kid’s username and password open only their own account and purchase form.
      Keep passwords private and reset any password that has been disclosed.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Passwords are checked by our server. Hosting, server functions, and the database run on Google Firebase. Those
      providers process data as needed to deliver their services under their own
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Data stays in the database while your account and family records exist. If
      you want your account or family data removed, contact the site operator
      using the link in the footer on the home page.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Kids may view their own balances and record purchases. Parents control
      each kid’s password and can disable sign-in. The app is meant for parents to
      manage allowance for their own children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes in a meaningful way, the date at the top of this page
      will be updated.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
